  "label": "Use of 'for example' as a rhetorical device",
  "description": "The phrase 'for example' is a common rhetorical tool used to introduce an illustration or instance that supports a general statement or argument. In this meme, it signals that the image is being used as a visual example to support a broader point — likely about diversity in education, the universality of studying, or the representation of people of color in academic settings. Understanding this rhetorical function requires knowledge of common language conventions outside the image.",
